title: Seat
---
<<if isTeacherDistracted()>>
    What do you want to do with the teacher distracted?

    -> Pump out an essay for Opitz. <<if hasActions()>>
        <<jump Essay>>
    -> Back
        <<stop>>

<<else>>
    What do you want to do during class?

    -> Pay attention. <<if hasActions()>>
        <<useAction>> 
        You pay attention to the lecture, Dr. Dickinson is pleased. 
    -> Cause a distraction. <<if hasActions() and GetPaper() > 0>>
        <<jump Distraction>>
    -> Back
        <<stop>>
<<endif>>

===
title: Distraction
---
<<useAction>>

<<if GetPaper() == 1>>
    You pull out the normal piece of paper.
    Teacher: Bruh... 
    Teacher: Get out of my class. 

<<elseif GetPaper() == 2>>
    You pull out the crumpled paper.
    Teacher: WHO THREW THAT?!
    <<PaperDistraction>>

<<endif>>

<<stop>>
===
title: Essay
---
<<useAction>>
You write up an essay to turn into Optiz in exchange for a chapel credit. 
Thats your first credit gained! 

<<stop>>
===

